From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ps4-gladius <ps4-gladius@invalid>
Date: Tue, 7 Oct 2026 20:50:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] server: share the descriptor for a mapping when dup is refused.

No descriptor can be duplicated on this console -- dup, dup2, fcntl(F_DUPFD)
and sceKernelRdup all fail, for regular files, directories, shm objects,
sockets and pipes alike (src/dup-probe). An fd with a name can be reopened
instead (0734); one without, which is the branch a mapping takes, cannot.

Sharing is already how this path prefers to work: get_fd_object_for_mapping
returns grab_object() whenever an fd with matching access and sharing exists,
and only falls through to dup_fd_object when none matches exactly. A mapping
never seeks -- it mmaps and nothing else -- so the file offset a duplicate
would have owned is never used. Take the original when duplication is refused.

Two things come with sharing rather than duplicating, and both took a run on
the console to find:

Leave the descriptor to its owner, as the sharing path above does. set_fd_user
asserts that an fd has no user yet, and one opened for another object already
has one; calling it aborted the server the first time a mapping of a real file
took this path. The earlier ones had no owner, so it stayed hidden.

Clear the error. dup_fd_object turns its errno into an NTSTATUS before it
returns -- EPERM becomes STATUS_ACCESS_DENIED -- so recovering the descriptor
without clearing it fails the request with the error of a call that no longer
matters. That is what refused to start the game, long after the mapping itself
had succeeded:

    wine: cannot run "C:\Games\Oblivion\Oblivion.exe" in this process:
          status c0000022
---
diff --git a/server/mapping.c b/server/mapping.c
--- a/server/mapping.c
+++ b/server/mapping.c
@@ -1135,7 +1135,34 @@ static bool mapping_init( struct object *obj, const void *init_data )
         if (!(mapping->fd = get_fd_object_for_mapping( data->fd, mapping_access, sharing )))
         {
             mapping->fd = dup_fd_object( data->fd, mapping_access, sharing, FILE_SYNCHRONOUS_IO_NONALERT );
+#ifdef __PROSPERO__
+            /* ⚠ No descriptor can be duplicated on this console (src/dup-probe:
+             * dup, dup2, fcntl(F_DUPFD) and sceKernelRdup all refused, for every
+             * kind of descriptor), and the fd that fails here -- the NLS file,
+             * opened by the server itself -- has no unix_name to reopen.
+             *
+             * Sharing is already how this path prefers to work:
+             * get_fd_object_for_mapping returns grab_object() whenever it finds
+             * an fd with matching access and sharing, and only falls here when
+             * none matches exactly. A mapping never seeks -- it mmaps and
+             * nothing else -- so the file offset a duplicate would have owned is
+             * never used. Take the original rather than fail. */
+#endif
             if (mapping->fd) set_fd_user( mapping->fd, &mapping_fd_ops, NULL );
+#ifdef __PROSPERO__
+            /* Take the original, and leave it to its owner exactly as the
+             * sharing path above does: set_fd_user asserts that an fd has no
+             * user yet, and this one belongs to the object it was opened for.
+             *
+             * dup_fd_object has already turned its errno into an NTSTATUS on
+             * the way out -- EPERM becomes STATUS_ACCESS_DENIED -- so clear it,
+             * or the request fails with the error of a call we just recovered
+             * from. That is what refused to start the game:
+             *
+             *     wine: cannot run "C:\Games\Oblivion\Oblivion.exe" in this
+             *           process: status c0000022 */
+            else if ((mapping->fd = (struct fd *)grab_object( data->fd ))) clear_error();
+#endif
         }
         if (!mapping->fd) return false;
 
